  "prompt_template": "You are an expert professional translator and translation quality annotator using the MQM (Multidimensional Quality Metrics) framework.\n\nAnnotate every error in the {target_lang} translation of the {source_lang} source below.\n\nFor each error give:\n- \"span\": the erroneous text copied from the translation (or \"\" for an omission)\n- \"category\": one of \"accuracy/mistranslation\", \"accuracy/omission\", \"accuracy/addition\", \"accuracy/untranslated\", \"fluency/grammar\", \"fluency/spelling\", \"fluency/punctuation\", \"fluency/register\", \"fluency/inconsistency\", \"style/awkward\", \"terminology/inappropriate\", \"non-translation\", \"other\"\n- \"severity\": \"minor\" (does not impede understanding) or \"major\" (changes or obscures meaning, or a serious fluency problem). Use category \"non-translation\" only when the output is not a translation of the source at all.\n\n{source_lang} source:\n{source}\n\n{target_lang} translation:\n{hypothesis}\n\nRespond with only a JSON object of the form {{\"errors\": [{{\"span\": \"...\", \"category\": \"...\", \"severity\": \"...\"}}]}}. Use {{\"errors\": []}} if the translation has no errors.",
  "prompt_template_sha256": "9f47501e0d6081b05a1a40fa601ffb8c67a8053d1013f662a7263816ecdcd324",
  "purpose": "Validate an LLM MQM judge as a proxy for human MQM when scoring outputs of reward-optimized MT policies.",
  "sample_seed": 20261104,
  "scoring": "Judge errors are scored with mqm_human_scores.error_penalty, the same weights as human MQM (major 5, minor 1, minor punctuation 0.1, non-translation 25); quality = -penalty. Unparseable outputs are counted, retried never, and excluded from analysis; parse rate is reported.",
  "segments_per_pool": 200,
  "status": "frozen_before_any_judge_output",
  "tests": {
    "T0_parse_rate": "fraction of candidates with a parseable JSON error list",
    "T1_within_source_pairwise_accuracy": "Over all candidate pairs sharing a source segment, tie-calibrated pairwise accuracy (acc_eq, Deutsch et al. 2023) of judge quality against human quality. Reported for every judge and for external QE rewards on the same candidates as reference points.",
    "T2_system_level_pearson": "Pearson of per-system mean judge vs human quality within each pool",
    "T3_selection_gain_agreement": "For every reward r available on a pool (all trained reward instances plus external QE controls) and each selection rule (top-1, exact expected best-of-4), compute the gain over the uniform-candidate mean in human quality and in judge quality. Units: within-pool z-scores of each quality measure. Uncertainty by segment bootstrap (2000 resamples, seed 20261104)."
  }
